    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Palau Chamber of Commerce  implemented  the Business Accelerator programme for 15 creative-prenuers  and supported the formalisation of 2 cooperatives for the creative-prenuers. The ILO in collaboration with the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organisation (UNESCO), United Nations Development Programme (UNDP), and the International Fund for Agricultural Development (IFAD) provided technical support promoting Inclusive Economic Recovery through Sustainable Enterprises in the Informal Economies of Fiji, Palau, Tonga and Vanuatu targeting informal sector enterprises and workers in the creative industries and the agriculture sector.   
The ILO mobilised stakeholders in the labour market, increased capacities to sustain enterprises and decent work, and improve access to markets as a way to address unemployment, underemployment, and business deficits to improve resilience and employment, production, and income recovery from the impacts of COVID-19. 
The formalisation of the 2 cooperatives also provided pathways and guidelines for registrations in the informal and creative sectors specific to the Palaun context.</narrative>
   </description>
